            <ArticleTitle>Review of the relationship between stress and wound healing: part 1.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While it has been suggested there is a link between stress and delayed wound healing, less is known about the role of pain as a contributor to stress. This paper reviews the evidence for this from studies of acute, surgical and chronic wounds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
